  message: "Fixed in PR #1747 (dev ad46a5071d). Verdicts, each read before acting: WIRED -- id_template_problem / edge_template_problem (scripts/check-id-construction ran private skeleton twins; it now hands each id as a {} template to the public classifiers, _edge_skeleton_problem deleted; spy test test_the_lint_asks_the_public_classifiers) and kind_for_yaml_section (the catalogue loader's three copy-pasted per-section loops with KIND_* written in are one loop over YAML_SECTIONS; spy test test_the_loader_takes_each_kind_from_the_section_registry). RETIRED -- resolve_arbitration_policy (the CLI takes policy_from_config(_load_config_or_exit(...)); spec line updated), write_boundary_for_target_kind (writes are consumed via _boundary_for_target_kind(kind, 'write') in boundary selection; every write boundary is a sink zone so a sink-side twin of the mint gate would never refuse), build_interface_impl_map (the linker reads _iter_interface_impls). KEPT, INV-hokin's 'designed consumer is a test' class -- get_analyzer (48 test call sites; WI-juzig removed its production use deliberately) and in_window (the module docstring names the scope-gate test as its consumer); both stay in the baseline. BEHAVIORAL: a fresh self-map of the merged tree (5m32s) run through scripts/check-test-only-reachability: exit 0, 'no new test-only-reachable functions', GATED cohort 293 = the shrunk baseline (301 -> 293: the 6 above plus run_analyzer and find_wolfram_files, which the gate reported no longer test-only); check-self-tree-validation exit 0; scripts/check-id-construction exit 0 on dev."  # 8f06
